[36m│[0m ### Red-drives that killed zero vectors, and why (real findings)             [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m - **`charges-wrong-rounding-half-even`** is a genuine, plausible defect      [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m (HALF_EVEN vs HALF_UP) but **indistinguishable on the corpus**: the captured [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m products carry no exact-half tie (FC-09's fraction is .55525; every other    [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m product is exact), so no stored fee lands on the .5 boundary where the two   [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m modes differ. The store grades truncation drift (see the pre-existing        [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m `charges-wrong-percent-truncating`, parity_fail=1) but cannot see a *mode    [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m substitution* that agrees everywhere except the un-captured tie. A permanent [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m probe-vector test proves the defect is real (an exact-half request rounds up [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m under HALF_UP, not under HALF_EVEN) — the corpus itself is blind to it.      [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m - **`charges-wrong-validation-skipped`** produces an identical answer on all [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m ten construction-*valid* charges, and the `fee_requires_valid` invariant     [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m cannot catch it because a skipped validation yields an *empty* validation    [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m list, which is the invariant's HOLD shape. The construction-validation       [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m refusal path (a penalty charge at disbursement that the oracle refuses) is   [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m simply **ungraded by the store**; the permanent probe test asserts the port  [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m charges a request the oracle refuses.                                        [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m                                                                              [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m Both zero-killers therefore do what a red-drive is for: they prove the       [36m│[0m
[36m│[0m *store* cannot see those defects, not that the defects are harmless.         [36m│[0m
